        "explanation": "<h3>The Maths of Money</h3><p>Real-world application of percentages.</p><h4>Profit & Loss</h4><ul><li><strong>Cost Price (CP):</strong> Buying price.</li><li><strong>Selling Price (SP):</strong> Selling price.</li><li><strong>Profit:</strong> SP - CP. (<strong>Loss</strong> is CP - SP).</li><li><strong>Profit %:</strong> (Profit / CP) × 100.</li></ul><h4>Interest</h4><ul><li><strong>Simple Interest (SI):</strong> P × R × T / 100. (Only principal earns interest).</li><li><strong>Compound Interest (CI):</strong> Interest earns interest! Growth is exponential.</li></ul>",
